		<SWE></SWE>
		<SWF></SWF>
		<Meldungstext>\T\C\S\K\Axxxxxxx\C\B\K\Ax  	\L\S\K\A(0=not active/1=active)\C\S\K\N
 \C\B\K\A      1: 	\L\B\K\ATop request\C\S\K\N
      2:  	\L\S\K\NTop enable\C\S\K\N
     3:   	blank
    4:    	Top open
   5:	     Top close
  6:			Blank
 7:				Window down
8:					Ambient conditions 								not OK\Y\F\J\N
 Y\Y\S\J\NZ\L\S\G\A\INote:\Y\S\K\N
 J\L\R\K\A\I The displayed CAN messages (bits 1-7) are not relevant to Service, but are intended for more detailed fault analysis.\Y\S\K\N
 J\L\S\K\I In response to a request to open/close the convertible top by way of the convenience system (via lock cylinder A\Y\S\K\N operating instructions) first bit4/bit 5 is set. If the ambient conditions are OK (bit 8) and the windows are down (bit 7) a convertible top request (bit 1) is issued. To finally start the convertible top motion after about 2 seconds, the top enable bit (Bit 2) is set.
 J\L\S\K\I Environmental conditions not OK - One of the functional requirements is not met (e.g. hardtop mounted, operating voltage NOK, abort by fault entry, software protective function active, etc.)\Y\S\K\N
 J\L\S\K\I At an ambient temperature &lt; -15°C only the -Close top- function is possible. </Meldungstext>
